From 8ad8a29c8e9df26e10ba9b6ecf6b8bece171ee9c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tao Xiaobai <1599170798@qq.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 13:34:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Little Craft Launcher: report game sessions to the host
 and fetch a compatible Java

- LclSession: the runtime's half of the host's session records. The entry
  activity always ends the hand-over it was given (starting, failed with the
  reason, or cancelled) and the game process keeps the session lock for its
  whole life, so the host can protect a running instance across restarts.
- A Java requirement that is not itself published (16 for Minecraft 1.17)
  now downloads the lowest published release that runs it instead of failing
  before any download.
- Plain JVM tests for both.
